---Decorative component that simply draws a text string onto the screen.
---
---This is mostly an extension of ui.TextData, with the only functionality besides what's provided by that and by
---`Component` being functionality to associate this component with an object, making it so the object's name is drawn
---instead of the normal component contents.
---@class ui.Text : ui.Component
---@field associatedObjectID integer Numeric ID for the object associated with this component, or -1 if no associated object exists.
---@field associatedObjectQuantity integer The quantity for the object associated with this component.
---@field content string The text to draw.
---@field font integer The font to use when drawing this text.
---@field alignHorizontal ui.AlignMode Horizontal alignment for this text.
---@field alignVertical ui.AlignMode Vertical alignment for this text.
---@field maxLines integer Maximum number of lines to display. Can be set to 0 to allow an unlimited number of lines.
---@field isShadowed boolean Whether or not to draw this text with a shadow effect for better legibility. Defaults to false.
ui.Text = {}

---Creates a new text component on the specified parent.
---
---Warning: Creating a component can fail if there's already a component on that parent with the same category ID and
---dynamic ID, or if those are omitted and the application is unable to generate a valid ID for the component.
---@param parent ui.ComponentCollection Parent component to create this text component in.
---@param categoryID? integer Category ID used to identify this component. Defaults to the parent's category ID if not specified.
---@param dynamicID? integer Dynamic ID used to identify this component. Defaults to auto-incrementing from the parent's dynamic ID if not specified.
---@return ui.Text # The newly created text component. The caller must set its layout and visual information afterwards.
function ui.Text.new(parent, categoryID, dynamicID) end

---Associates an object with this component, making it use the object's name and optionally it's quantity as the
---displayed contents for this component.
---@param objectID integer Numeric ID for the object to associate with this component.
---@param quantity? Long The quantity for the object to associate with this component.
function ui.Text:SetAssociatedObject(objectID, quantity) end

---Sets the alignment for this text.
---@param alignment ui.AlignMode The alignment to set as both horizontal and vertical alignments.
---@overload fun(self: ui.Text, horizontalAlignment: ui.AlignMode, verticalAlignment: ui.AlignMode)
function ui.Text:AlignTo(alignment) end

---Sets this Text's properties based on the provided config values.
---@param config ui.TextDataConfig The config to source the various properties from.
function ui.Text:SetConfig(config) end

---Returns a copy of this Text's config, allowing it to be used elsewhere.
---@return ui.TextDataConfig # Config containing a copy of all properties set on this Text object, excluding non-config properties (eg. `content`)
function ui.Text:GetConfigCopy() end
